   "answer": "Naproxen is not listed as a contraindication for lisinopril, but the naproxen label warns that NSAIDs \u201cmay have impaired response to\u2026 ACE inhibitors\u201d and that blood pressure should be monitored when an NSA\u202fID is started in a patient taking an ACE inhibitor.\u202fThus the drugs can be taken together, but the combination may reduce the antihypertensive effect of lisinopril and requires blood\u2011pressure monitoring.  \n\n**Sources**  \n- openFDA label: Naproxen \u2014 Warnings (NSAIDs may impair response to ACE inhibitors)  \n- openFDA label: Lisinopril \u2014 Contraindications (no NSA\u2011ID contraindication)",
